Despite such a message in Nethack in certain circumstances, sickness
is not only "contaminated fruit juice" if you consider the application
to poison projectiles. But I suspect you're arguing the word "unspecific"
WRT Nethack while I've done WRT Real Life.

WRT "more than" I suppose we can split hairs on that question and won't
reach anywhere. I don't say you are wrong, but "more than" is quite
meaningless, I'd say. Okay, let's handle it more verbose...

  water: unique - but there's the isotope variants of H2O; D2O and T2O.
  fruit juice: all kinds of fruits (all water based? at least cell water)
  oil: hmm.. - there are thousands of oils; in Nethack oil may be lamp
               oil, or weapon oil, or oil fitting for molotov coctails
               (which would rather be something easier flammable in RL)
  acid: there are thousands of acids; but reaction with water suggests
               that it is vitriol, so we may assume it's unique
  booze: many RL variants, but unique main component; ethanol
  sickness: thousands of possibilities

Now lets add potion classes that are classified as magical...

  healing, extra healing, full healing: many possibilities but nothing
               really comparable with RL medicine (given what it heals)
  hallucination, confusion: quite a couple possibilities

But all that is quite an academic and/or rather artificial elaboration.

